 "label": "PROVISIONAL_ASR_NOT_LISTENING",
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.28,
   "text": "What would be the cumulative energy of the hundreds of thousands of keystrokes required",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 3.28,
   "end": 3.98,
   "text": "to write a novel?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 4.5,
   "end": 7.68,
   "text": "There's a lot of engineering research into the force required to press keys, in part",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 7.68,
   "end": 10.12,
   "text": "because so many people suffer from repetitive strain injuries.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 10.48,
   "end": 13.78,
   "text": "Using data from a study of rubber dome keyboards, we can estimate that the energy required",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 13.78,
   "end": 18.1,
   "text": "to press a key is around 1.5 millijoules for a letter key and 2.5 for a big key like",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 18.1,
   "end": 19.08,
   "text": "enter or spacebar.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 19.42,
   "end": 21.02,
   "text": "How much is 1.5 millijoules?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 21.24,
   "end": 23.84,
   "text": "Well, it's enough to heat a drop of water by 1% of a degree.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 24.16,
   "end": 28.36,
   "text": "It's also enough to lift a squirrel 300 microns all the way from the ground to the",
   "avg_logprob": -0.125,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.001
  },
  {
   "start": 28.36,
   "end": 29.7,
   "text": "stack of four sheets of paper.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 30.16,
   "end": 33.74,
   "text": "A typical novel might have half a million to a million characters in it, so typing it out",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 33.74,
   "end": 35.36,
   "text": "would require at least that many key presses.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 36.06,
   "end": 39.02,
   "text": "The amount of backspacing and rewriting varies wildly from person to person.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 39.3,
   "end": 42.12,
   "text": "Some people write straight through without pausing your editing, while others rewrite",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 42.12,
   "end": 43.0,
   "text": "every sentence endlessly.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 43.62,
   "end": 46.04,
   "text": "It turns out not to make a big difference which kind of writer you are.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 46.26,
   "end": 49.08,
   "text": "If you write straight through without editing, you'd expend about a kilojoule.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 49.32,
   "end": 52.4,
   "text": "With a lot of rewrites, you might expend several kilojoules, but you'd need to",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 52.4,
   "end": 56.36,
   "text": "rewrite every word ten times to match the energy stored in a single AA battery.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.108,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.147
  },
  {
   "start": 57.0,
   "end": 60.74,
   "text": "Writing one full novel would provide enough energy to run a laptop for a total of about",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 60.74,
   "end": 61.66,
   "text": "30 seconds.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 62.0,
   "end": 65.26,
   "text": "If each novel takes you six months, you'd spend two seconds out of every million",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 65.26,
   "end": 66.38,
   "text": "running off keyboard power.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 66.96,
   "end": 70.34,
   "text": "A novel every six months seems like a lot of typing, but plenty of people type more.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 70.66,
   "end": 73.88,
   "text": "If you abandon the requirement of writing actual words and just care about the most",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 73.88,
   "end": 76.34,
   "text": "key presses, esports is a promising place to look.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 76.76,
   "end": 80.76,
   "text": "Top esports professionals can clock in over 400 actions per minute, which are a mix of",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 80.76,
   "end": 81.9,
   "text": "mouse clicks and keystrokes.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 82.1,
   "end": 85.62,
   "text": "Taking a conservative estimate, a top esports player types the equivalent of a novel in",
   "avg_logprob": -0.129,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.048
  },
  {
   "start": 85.62,
   "end": 86.86,
   "text": "a few days of playing time.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.024
  },
  {
   "start": 87.36,
   "end": 90.82,
   "text": "However, a few days still isn't fast enough to represent much energy.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.024
  },
  {
   "start": 91.38,
   "end": 94.28,
   "text": "Remember, to keep a laptop running from keypress power alone, you'd need to write",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.024
  },
  {
   "start": 94.28,
   "end": 95.44,
   "text": "a novel in half a minute.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.024
  },
  {
   "start": 95.8,
   "end": 99.3,
   "text": "Even for the fastest typists, writing is not a novel form of exercise.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.144,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.024
  }
 ],
